' 0. Parties
' Who does what, and who calls or reads whom, on a high level.
' The protocol numbers point to the files that detail each party.

@startuml parties

left to right direction
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #d1d5ef
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #ffffff
}

actor "operator" as Operator
actor "auditor" as Auditor

rectangle "Files" #LightBlue {
  database settings [
    **settings**
    ----
    client, hosts and their server addresses,
    keys: placeholder, allowed host, bound header
  ]
  database secrets [
    **secrets**
    ----
    the real key values, by key name
  ]
}

rectangle "Sandbox" #LightBlue {
  rectangle program [
    **program**
    ----
    calls APIs with placeholders
  ]
}

rectangle "Tally proxy" #LightBlue {
  rectangle proxy [
    **proxy** (1, 3, 4, 5)
    ----
    checks the files at startup
    decides each request
    swaps placeholders for real keys
    forwards requests, relays responses
  ]
  rectangle writer [
    **writer** (2)
    ----
    the log's only writer
    numbers each line
    forces it to disk, then answers
  ]
  database log [
    **log**
    ----
    one file per run, from start line to stop line
    one line per decision or upstream error, append-only
  ]
}

rectangle "Upstream" #LightBlue {
  rectangle server [
    **server**
    ----
    the real API
  ]
}

rectangle "Audit" #LightBlue {
  rectangle checker [
    **checker** (6)
    ----
    re-checks the log against the settings
  ]
}

Operator --> proxy : starts, stops
program --> proxy : requests with placeholders;\ngets responses or refusals
proxy --> settings : reads
proxy --> secrets : reads
proxy --> writer : logs every decision (2)
writer --> log : appends, forces to disk
proxy --> server : requests with real keys;\ngets responses
Auditor --> checker : runs
checker --> log : reads
checker --> settings : reads

@enduml
